;; SRFI 1 (list library): where scheme/lib/srfi/%3a1/lists.sls comes from (SM6)
[{:file "scheme/lib/srfi/%3a1/lists.sls"
  :repo "https://github.com/scheme-requests-for-implementation/srfi-1" :commit "72442d67896181afccd4519c36140ba65ccfd0ca"
  :path "srfi-1-reference.scm" :sha256 "2cb6216a0780cecee63dcabec91ffe0e76ec9de2fdf98ab1d564d4129bed8e6b"
  :license "MIT; Olin Shivers' notice kept at the top (LICENSE.md, SRFI 1)"
  :changes "Wrapped as an R6RS library (export list from the reference's header). The definitions of cons*, filter, partition and find are removed: (rnrs lists)'s are exported instead. map, member, assoc, fold-right and remove are the reference's (SRFI 1's, not R6RS's). Added: ERROR as a wrapper over R6RS's error (who #f), CHECK-ARG, RECEIVE, :OPTIONAL and LET-OPTIONALS (the reference leaves them to the system), set-car!/set-cdr! from (rnrs mutable-pairs). Everything else is the reference's text. The tests (test/scheme/srfi/srfi-1.sps) are written for the port: the repository has no tests."}]
